% The traditional wolf, goat and cabbage puzzle has a farmer and a small boat.
% The boat carries the farmer and at most one item; the goat may not stay
% with the wolf or the cabbage without the farmer.
% Finds both plans that move everyone across within seven crossings.
% Shows states as lists, repeated variables in a pattern, safety by
% alternatives and bounded recursive planning.

the templates are:
    *a bank* is opposite *a bank*,
    *a state* is safe,
    *a state* moves to *a state* carrying *a cargo*,
    *a plan* takes the crew from *a state* to the left bank in at most *a number* crossings.

the knowledge base river crossing includes:

right is opposite left.
left is opposite right.

% A state lists the banks of the farmer F, the wolf W, the goat G and the
% cabbage C. It is safe when the farmer is with the goat, or the goat is
% alone with neither the wolf nor the cabbage.
a state is safe
    if the state = [F, W, G, C]
    and F = G
        or W is different from G
            and G is different from C.

% The farmer crosses alone or with an item on the farmer's bank.
a state moves to an other state carrying nothing
    if the state = [F, W, G, C]
    and F is opposite a bank B
    and the other state = [B, W, G, C].

a state moves to an other state carrying wolf
    if the state = [F, F, G, C]
    and F is opposite a bank B
    and the other state = [B, B, G, C].

a state moves to an other state carrying goat
    if the state = [F, W, F, C]
    and F is opposite a bank B
    and the other state = [B, W, B, C].

a state moves to an other state carrying cabbage
    if the state = [F, W, G, F]
    and F is opposite a bank B
    and the other state = [B, W, G, B].

% A plan is the list of what each crossing carries.
a plan takes the crew from a state to the left bank in at most a number N crossings
    if the state = [left, left, left, left]
    and the plan = [].

a plan takes the crew from a state to the left bank in at most a number N crossings
    if N > 0
    and the state moves to a next state carrying a cargo
    and the next state is safe
    and a number M = N - 1
    and a rest takes the crew from the next state to the left bank in at most M crossings
    and the plan has the cargo as head before the rest.

query plans is:
    which plan takes the crew from [right, right, right, right] to the left bank in at most 7 crossings.
